From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:10:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: decode VP9 up to 8192x8192

The VP9 coded format was capped at 4096x4096 since the driver was
added. The decoder does more: on the M4 (T8132) macOS decodes VP9
profile 0 and profile 2 at 7680x4320 on this hardware. Every VP9
working buffer is already sized from the frame's own width and height,
the tile code handles the 16 tile columns VP9 allows, and the frame
size goes to the hardware in the same 16-bit fields that AV1 uses at
8K.

Raise the VP9 frame size limit to 8192x8192. H.264 stays at 4096x4096.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c
index 4481917e94..0b6df1c44b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c
@@ -460,10 +460,10 @@ static const struct avd_coded_fmt_desc avd_coded_fmts[] = {
 		.fourcc = V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME,
 		.frmsize = {
 			.min_width = 64,
-			.max_width = 4096,
+			.max_width = 8192,
 			.step_width = 64,
 			.min_height = 64,
-			.max_height = 4096,
+			.max_height = 8192,
 			.step_height = 16,
 		},
 		.ctrls = &avd_vp9_ctrls,
-- 
2.43.0

